WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.465
[SINGING IN LATIN]

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:33.400
LARRY ARNN: The Psalmist
writes, "unless the Lord

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.453
builds the house, those who
build it labor in vain."

00:00:37.453 --> 00:00:40.120
We have cause to think that this
is the largest classical chapel

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.110
built in 70 years.

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:46.450
The question is not
why have we built this.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:49.210
When you walk in here,
don't you look up and think

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:50.975
of the ultimate things?

00:00:50.975 --> 00:00:52.600
The answer to that
question is obvious.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.350
The hard question is,
why have others not?

00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:59.980
I think it is a turning away
from things that are beautiful,

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:03.860
which means necessarily then
also things that are true

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:05.747
and things that are good.

00:01:05.747 --> 00:01:07.330
When the truth and
the beauty and good

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:10.700
are gone, then, of
course, all reasons

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:13.970
that demand we strive to become
good human beings are gone.

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:16.610
It is actually the purpose of
the activity of the College

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:18.800
to explain and
understand all that.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:25.610
And that activity goes on
intensely now for 175 years.

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:27.790
CLARENCE THOMAS: This is
a very special occasion,

00:01:27.790 --> 00:01:32.650
175th anniversary of
Hillsdale and the dedication

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:34.710
of this beautiful chapel.

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:39.610
The chapel's enduring beauty
highlights the transcendence,

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:42.880
sovereignty, and
the grace of God.

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:47.260
It truly illustrates
how architectural design

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:52.273
can reflect the character of God
and evoke a sense of reverence

00:01:52.273 --> 00:01:52.940
for His majesty.

00:01:57.462 --> 00:01:58.920
PATRICK SAJAK:
You're going to hear

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:00.900
a lot in the coming
months about the four

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.670
purposes of this college--

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:06.790
learning, character,
faith, and freedom.

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:09.270
These are the principles of
education here at Hillsdale,

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:11.970
have been for 175
years, and we hope

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:15.920
it will be another 175 years.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:19.380
LARRY ARNN: We live
in an age of confusion

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:23.870
that has become dangerous
threatening tyranny.

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:29.330
The only thing ultimately that
can dispel it is understanding.

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:33.750
This college was
born 175 years ago

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.920
to give that
understanding wherever

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:39.420
anybody wanted to learn.

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:47.510
You and God have given us
the means to make that big.

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:48.010
Thank you.

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:51.360
[APPLAUSE]

